guided.response:
The right Scale component here is **`sc-tabs`** — a WAI-ARIA APG tabbed interface that manages selection, focus, and panel visibility. It pairs `sc-tab` triggers with `sc-tab-panel` content areas.

### Imports

```js
import '@scale-ds/scale-design-system/components/sc-tabs';
import '@scale-ds/scale-design-system/components/sc-tab';
import '@scale-ds/scale-design-system/components/sc-tab-panel';
```

### Markup

```html
<sc-tabs>
  <!-- Tab triggers -->
  <sc-tab slot="tabs" panel="overview">Overview</sc-tab>
  <sc-tab slot="tabs" panel="settings">Settings</sc-tab>
  <sc-tab slot="tabs" panel="activity">Activity</sc-tab>

  <!-- Matching panels -->
  <sc-tab-panel name="overview">
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>Summary of your account and recent highlights.</p>
  </sc-tab-panel>

  <sc-tab-panel name="settings">
    <h2>Settings</h2>
    <p>Manage preferences, notifications, and integrations.</p>
  </sc-tab-panel>

  <sc-tab-panel name="activity">
    <h2>Activity</h2>
    <p>A timeline of actions taken in your workspace.</p>
  </sc-tab-panel>
</sc-tabs>
```

### How it works

| Concept | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Pairing** | Each `sc-tab`'s `panel` attribute matches the `name` attribute on its `sc-tab-panel`. |
| **Slot** | Tab triggers go in `slot="tabs"`. Panels are default-slotted children. |
| **Default selection** | The first tab is selected automatically. To change, add `selected` to another `sc-tab`. |
| **Keyboard** | Arrow keys move focus between tabs; Enter/Space activates. Fully WAI-ARIA compliant out of the box. |

### Styling with tokens

```css
/* Spacing around each panel's content */
sc-tab-panel {
  padding-block: var(--sc-spacing-24);
}

sc-tab-panel h2 {
  font: var(--sc-typography-heading-m);
  color: var(--sc-color-text-primary);
  margin-block-end: var(--sc-spacing-8);
}

sc-tab-panel p {
  font: var(--sc-typography-body-m);
  color: var(--sc-color-text-secondary);
}
```

This gives you three in-page views switchable without a page navigation, with full keyboard and screen-reader support handled by the component.

