- **`sc-file-upload`** — Drag-and-drop upload zone with per-file progress, error states, and single/multiple file support
- **`sc-file-upload-item`** — A single file row showing name, size, progress bar, and status with a remove control

> ⚠️ **Note:** I could not verify the exact prop names and enum values from the guidance files. Before shipping, please run `get-component-guidance` for `sc-file-upload` and `sc-file-upload-item` (or read their `.md` files in `node_modules/@scale-ds/scale-design-system/context/agents/`) to confirm the API. The code below follows Scale naming conventions and the catalog descriptions.

---

### Imports

```js
import '@scale-ds/scale-design-system/components/sc-file-upload';
import '@scale-ds/scale-design-system/components/sc-file-upload-item';
```

### Global stylesheet (once per app)

```scss
@use '@scale-ds/scale-design-system/scss/main';
```

### HTML — Multi-file drag-and-drop with per-file progress

```html
<sc-file-upload
  id="uploader"
  multiple
  label="Upload files"
  helper-text="Drag and drop files here, or click to browse"
  accept=".pdf,.png,.jpg,.docx"
  max-file-size="10"
>
</sc-file-upload>
```

### JavaScript — Handle drops, simulate upload, show per-file progress

```js
const uploader = document.querySelector('#uploader');

uploader.addEventListener('sc-change', (e) => {
  const files = e.detail?.files ?? e.target.files;
  if (!files?.length) return;

  Array.from(files).forEach((file) => {
    uploadFile(file);
  });
});

function uploadFile(file) {
  // Create a file-upload-item for visual per-file progress
  const item = document.createElement('sc-file-upload-item');
  item.fileName = file.name;
  item.fileSize = file.size;
  item.status = 'uploading';
  item.progress = 0;

  // Allow the user to cancel / remove
  item.addEventListener('sc-remove', () => {
    if (item._xhr) item._xhr.abort();
    item.remove();
  });

  uploader.appendChild(item);

  // Real upload via XMLHttpRequest for progress tracking
  const xhr = new XMLHttpRequest();
  item._xhr = xhr;

  xhr.upload.addEventListener('progress', (event) => {
    if (event.lengthComputable) {
      item.progress = Math.round((event.loaded / event.total) * 100);
    }
  });

  xhr.addEventListener('load', () => {
    if (xhr.status >= 200 && xhr.status < 300) {
      item.progress = 100;
      item.status = 'positive';   // success
    } else {
      item.status = 'negative';   // error
    }
  });

  xhr.addEventListener('error', () => {
    item.status = 'negative';
  });

  const formData = new FormData();
  formData.append('file', file);

  xhr.open('POST', '/api/upload');
  xhr.send(formData);
}
```

### What this gives you

| Feature | How it's handled |
|---|---|
| **Drag & drop** | Built into `sc-file-upload` — the drop zone, hover highlight, and file browse button are all native |
| **Per-file progress** | Each `sc-file-upload-item` renders the file name, size, a progress bar (0–100), and a status icon |
| **Error states** | Setting `status="negative"` on an item shows the error treatment |
| **Remove / cancel** | The `sc-remove` event fires when the user clicks the remove control; we abort the XHR and remove the item |
| **File restrictions** | `accept` limits file types; `max-file-size` (MB) limits size — the component handles validation UI |

### Styling overrides (tokens only)

If you need to adjust spacing or width around the uploader:

```css
sc-file-upload {
  --sc-file-upload-max-width: 40rem;
  margin-block: var(--sc-spacing-16);
}
```

